<title>UK: Cazenove Indian GDR Index dips.</title>
<headline>Cazenove Indian GDR Index dips.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cazenove Indian GDR Index fell 3.93 percent, or 3.07 points, to 75.09 on Monday after the Bombay Stock Exchange 30 share index dropped just over 79 points to 3,360.43.</p>
<p>The premium for GDRs over stocks on the local market was 15.23 percent.</p>
<p>The Cazenove index is a capitalisation weighted basket of Indian global depositary receipts and measures the change from midday on the previous trading day to midday today.</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Thatcher, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7770</p>
